{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Elohim called the light Day</b> — it tells that time was created and He made the measure of day and the measure of night. The sense of \"and He called\" is because man gave the names; regarding these that were made before he existed, it says that Elohim called their names — and this is the opinion of Rabbi Abraham. But the correct view is that the sense of \"calling\" in these instances here is the demarcation set in them when they assumed their form, and thus they said (Genesis Rabbah 3:6): \"Day shall be your boundary, and night shall be your boundary.\"" "<b>And it was evening and it was morning, one day</b> — there was evening and there was morning of one day. The beginning of night is called \"עֶרֶב\" because in it the forms intermingle (מִתְעָרְבוֹת), and the beginning of day is called \"בֹקֶר\" because a person examines (מְבַקֵּר) among them — thus Rabbi Abraham explained (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 1:5). And by way of the plain sense, it is not possible to say \"first day,\" because the second had not yet been made, since \"first\" precedes \"second\" either in number or in rank, but both must exist; whereas \"one\" does not imply a second. And there are those who explain (Guide for the Perplexed II:30) that this is an allusion to the rotation of the sphere over the entire earth in twenty-four hours, such that every moment of them is morning in changing places and evening in the places opposite them. And if so, it alludes to that which will be in the firmament after the luminaries are set in the firmament of the heavens."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "I rendered 'הַנָּכוֹן' as 'the correct view' following Ramban's standard usage when presenting his own position against Ibn Ezra's.", 1 "The phrase 'וְעַל דֶּרֶךְ הַפְּשָׁט' is rendered 'by way of the plain sense.' The closing clause about the firmament is translated hyper-literally; the referent of 'it' and the exact force of the allusion is left as Ramban leaves it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:12:09.463925390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}